00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.590 align:start position:0%
the european union's three main  institutions have clinched a deal on the  eu's budget for the next seven years  once endorsed by member states and the  european parliament it will provide some  960 billion euros for the 2014 to 2020  period with the focus on promoting  economic growth and jobs  this is a an important day for 500  million citizens it's also an important  day for the 26 million people who are  unemployed in this union and what we now  have to do in ratifying this political  agreement  by the institutions is to see that these  monies are channeled into effective  programs so that people all over this  union have the opportunity to have jobs  and careers as a consequence  a big slice of the package could be  front loaded onto the budget in the  first two years to tackle rampant youth  unemployment  the money could be injected into  apprenticeship schemes and small  businesses as well as research and the  erasmus lifelong learning program  the budget known as the multi-annual  financial framework is used to bring  europe's poorest regions into line with  their partners finance agricultural  spending infrastructure and education as  well as provide assistance to non-eu  nations  the institutions have pledged to  officially endorse the package by july  9.
 

